# API reference

Everything a script reaches outside plain Lua is in the `nml` table.

## By use

| For | |
|:----|:-|
| Content | `nml.element`, `nml.parse` — [[elements#]] |
| Reacting to elements | `nml.on` — [[elements#events]] |
| Later content | `nml.post_parse`, `nml.defer`, `nml.pages` — [[deferred#]] |
| Syntax | `nml.rule` and its atoms — [[rules#]] |
| The outside | `nml.read`, `nml.env`, `nml.time`, `nml.date`, `nml.variable` — [[lua#sandbox]] |
| Tables | `nml.tables` — [[tables#scripts|tables for scripts]] |

## Declarations

The declarations of the API, as [LuaLS](https://luals.github.io) reads them: `nml init` writes them to `.nml/types/nml.lua`, for editors. They are made from NML's own bindings, so they are always those of the `nml` that built this page.

:lua`nml.element("code_block", { code = nml.read("/.nml/types/nml.lua"), language = "lua", numbers = false })`
